  └────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────┘

  [38;5;153malerts.js[39m and [38;5;153mstore.js[39m never import UI; UI never imports storage. [38;5;153mmain.js[39m is the only module that knows about both,
  and it's the only one that calls [38;5;153mDate.now()[39m.

  [1mTooling[0m — cheapest to set up now, before any code exists. My recommendation is the first two:

  - [1mESLint + Prettier[0m — standard, catches real bugs in untyped JS.
  - [1mVitest[0m — unit tests; runs ES modules in Node with no browser, which the pure-function design is built for.
  - [1mPlaywright (e2e)[0m — real browser coverage of localStorage + rendering. Genuinely useful but a heavier dependency for
    an app this size.
  - [1mFuzz/property testing[0m — I'd skip it; the input space here is small and boundary cases are better enumerated by hand.

